WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.743 --> 00:00:03.190
(chuckles)

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:04.180
- [Mark] All right, so Lin.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.491
What's the latest?

00:00:05.491 --> 00:00:07.090
You were back in jail again?

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:07.923
- [Lin] Yeah.

00:00:07.923 --> 00:00:08.756
- [Mark] What happened?

00:00:08.756 --> 00:00:09.589
- Um.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.080
I ended up

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:16.900
on meth again

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.000
and I was on my comedown and I just,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.140
I got, I don't want to go into specifics,

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.380
but I got another charge,

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.243
and it's not looking too good, but I'm

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.820
trying my best to get
everything I need right now.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:40.150
I already have things set up

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:41.800
to get my ID back and everything.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:44.860
- [Mark] So you have
another hearing coming up?

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:45.693
- Yeah.

00:00:45.693 --> 00:00:46.553
- [Mark] For this case,

00:00:46.553 --> 00:00:48.410
and then there's also the previous one?

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:49.830
- Yeah.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:50.910
- [Mark] When is your next hearing.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:51.743
- On the ninth.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.326
- [Mark] So next week?

00:00:54.326 --> 00:00:55.759
- Yeah.

00:00:55.759 --> 00:00:56.592
Yeah.

00:00:56.592 --> 00:00:57.460
- [Mark] Make sure you don't miss it.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:58.314
- Yeah.

00:00:58.314 --> 00:00:59.147
All right.

00:00:59.147 --> 00:00:59.980
- [Mark] You don't want to do that.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:00.813
- No.

00:01:02.358 --> 00:01:04.080
- [Mark] So you've been
in jail before, right?

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:04.933
Like in Florida?

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:06.950
- Yeah.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.490
- [Mark] And that was for again,

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:10.800
some kind of violence?

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.110
- It was just all a bunch
of misunderstandings,

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.623
but I'm really not violent.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.090
I mean I wasn't violent there,

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:18.893
I'm not really a violent person.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.710
I think it's just like
the drugs and everything.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:26.030
I didn't do drugs in Florida, ever.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:27.347
- [Mark] Oh you didn't?

00:01:27.347 --> 00:01:28.180
Okay.
- No.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.720
- [Mark] But this last case was,

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:31.770
you stabbed somebody?

00:01:32.885 --> 00:01:33.718
- Yeah.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.693
- [Mark] And I'm sure
there were details on that

00:01:37.693 --> 00:01:39.023
that led to that, right?

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:42.120
- Yeah.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:42.970
Yeah, there were.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:48.083
- [Mark] How long were
you in jail this time?

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:54.083
- I was in there for
about a week, I think.

00:01:59.604 --> 00:02:01.544
- [Mark] And then Ben and
I bailed you out again.

00:02:01.544 --> 00:02:03.204
- Yeah, thank you guys.

00:02:03.204 --> 00:02:04.037
- [Mark] That's what we did.

00:02:04.037 --> 00:02:04.870
- Thank you guys for that.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:06.533
I haven't actually been
getting into any trouble.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:16.930
I haven't been getting into any trouble.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:17.930
- [Mark] Yeah, every time I've seen you,

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:20.950
you've seemed stable

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.587
and level-headed.
- Yeah.

00:02:23.587 --> 00:02:25.047
Yeah.

00:02:25.047 --> 00:02:26.835
- [Mark] But I'm sure drugs and alcohol

00:02:26.835 --> 00:02:28.920
might change that sometimes, right?

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:29.753
- Yeah.

00:02:29.753 --> 00:02:30.586
- [Mark] Is that typically
how your problems

00:02:30.586 --> 00:02:32.883
come about, is the drugs and the alcohol?

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:34.773
- Yeah.

00:02:34.773 --> 00:02:35.711
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:02:35.711 --> 00:02:36.544
- It is.

00:02:36.544 --> 00:02:40.223
It's the comedown from the meth,

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.270
mixed with alcohol,

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:47.555
combining also the mental
illnesses that people have,

00:02:47.555 --> 00:02:48.873
it's not good.

00:02:48.873 --> 00:02:51.552
I mean, I wouldn't advise
anybody to do that, you know?

00:02:51.552 --> 00:02:52.802
- [Mark] Right.

00:02:55.553 --> 00:02:57.670
So you recognize you
have some mental issues,

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:59.630
and then there's also the drug use.

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:00.463
- Yeah.

00:03:00.463 --> 00:03:02.220
- [Mark] And that whole
combination is just a--

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.053
- Yeah.

00:03:03.053 --> 00:03:03.886
- [Mark] A cocktail for trouble, right?

00:03:03.886 --> 00:03:04.719
- Mm-hmm.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:06.583
Yup.

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:09.900
- [Mark] You talk to your mom at all?

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:10.940
Does she know what's going on?

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:11.773
- Yeah.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.850
We're actually kind of getting along now.

00:03:22.217 --> 00:03:23.660
Yeah.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:24.593
- [Mark] That's good.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:31.470
So your future hinges on
how this court hearing goes

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.303
in the next two weeks.
- Yes.

00:03:32.303 --> 00:03:33.330
- [Mark] You have one this week coming up

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:34.530
and when's the next one?

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:37.449
- I'm not sure.

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:40.090
I guess I'll just have to

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:42.630
go to the courthouse
at some point this week

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:46.780
before the fourth, and
actually I should probably

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:48.290
do that either today or tomorrow,

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:49.373
go to the courthouse.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.440
Just to look up my cases and everything.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:55.273
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:55.273 --> 00:03:56.220
You don't want to screw that up.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.053
- No, I don't.

00:03:57.053 --> 00:03:59.090
I actually do need another co-signer

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:02.660
for the bail bonds,

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:04.670
because Ben didn't,

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:06.720
he didn't co-sign.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:07.983
He took his co-sign off.

00:04:10.696 --> 00:04:11.529
So.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:16.153
- [Mark] So you're living,

00:04:16.153 --> 00:04:18.850
what is your attraction
to Hollywood Boulevard?

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:19.810
You're living on the street.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:22.490
- There really is no attraction anymore.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:23.660
I just don't know where else to go.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.920
I've been trying to explore
the rest of Hollywood

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.263
and everything, and I've
been doing pretty good.

00:04:30.973 --> 00:04:33.210
I mean, it's not safe on the Boulevard.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.540
Not safe on the Boulevard
anymore at night especially.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:36.870
- [Mark] Yeah, somebody
slashed up your tent

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:37.703
you told me?

00:04:37.703 --> 00:04:38.813
- Yeah, somebody did.

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:42.750
- [Mark] I just got you that tent.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:43.704
- I know.

00:04:43.704 --> 00:04:44.537
It was in the first night.

00:04:44.537 --> 00:04:45.370
- [Mark] It's a pretty good tent.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:46.360
It lasted a night.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:48.290
- Yeah, it did.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:49.480
Yeah.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:52.160
But I fixed it.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.440
So, I'm gonna go to the store

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:57.160
and get fishing wire and fishing hook

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:58.960
because it holds better than thread.

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:01.470
- [Mark] Okay.

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:02.303
Got it.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:04.613
There's always little tricks

00:05:04.613 --> 00:05:06.240
of living on the street, aren't there?

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.073
- Huh?

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:07.906
- [Mark] There's always little tricks

00:05:07.906 --> 00:05:08.739
of living on the street.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:10.993
No?

00:05:10.993 --> 00:05:11.826
- Nope.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.780
- [Mark] So where do you think

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:20.810
if you end up not going to jail,

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:24.423
prison, whatever, what do
you plan on doing from here?

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:33.593
- I plan on getting an apartment.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:41.373
Maybe just saving up for a vehicle.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:46.277
And actually might move
out of LA at some point,

00:05:46.277 --> 00:05:48.770
because you know the
crime rate has gone up

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:52.050
and everything, and oh
actually I might have a job.

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:52.883
- [Mark] Where at?

00:05:52.883 --> 00:05:54.608
- A wig shop.

00:05:54.608 --> 00:05:55.487
- [Mark] Oh really?

00:05:55.487 --> 00:05:56.320
- Yeah.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:57.153
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:05:57.153 --> 00:05:57.986
- Yeah.

00:05:57.986 --> 00:05:59.060
If I can get that job, though,

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:02.110
I'll probably just like
save up and everything.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:04.753
- [Mark] That's great.

00:06:04.753 --> 00:06:06.180
- Start renting hotel rooms

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:08.130
where I'm actually safe and everything.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:10.960
Yeah.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:11.870
- [Mark] Excellent.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:14.843
Well I hope that works out.

00:06:14.843 --> 00:06:17.260
I hope the court case works out.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.093
- Yeah.

00:06:18.093 --> 00:06:18.926
- [Mark] Court cases.

00:06:18.926 --> 00:06:23.926
And I think staying away
from the drugs and alcohol

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:27.360
might be first on my list
of things you should do.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.671
- Yeah.

00:06:28.671 --> 00:06:30.160
I have actually been staying away

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.670
from alcohol and drugs.

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:32.510
- [Mark] Yeah, every time I've seen you

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:34.480
you seem sober as a judge, so.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.375
- Yeah.

00:06:35.375 --> 00:06:36.470
- [Mark] That's great.

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:37.303
- Yeah.

00:06:37.303 --> 00:06:38.418
- [Mark] All right, well
good luck next week.

00:06:38.418 --> 00:06:39.508
- All right, thank you.

00:06:39.508 --> 00:06:40.841
- [Mark] Thanks.

00:06:58.107 --> 00:06:59.403
All right Lin.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:01.213
Lin.

00:07:02.157 --> 00:07:04.800
So you just had your hearing this morning.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:07.210
And it went well?

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:08.043
- Yeah.

00:07:08.043 --> 00:07:08.975
- [Mark] You're smiling.

00:07:08.975 --> 00:07:09.808
- Yeah.

00:07:09.808 --> 00:07:10.641
Yeah.

00:07:10.641 --> 00:07:12.320
(chuckles) It went very well.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:13.430
- [Mark] So this was the hearing

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.090
for the stabbing, right?-

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:16.268
- Uh, yeah.

00:07:16.268 --> 00:07:20.670
- [Mark] And so what
does this mean for you?

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.210
Now you'll be free for a while,

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:23.203
or free forever?

00:07:24.792 --> 00:07:26.490
- I think it means

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:28.020
I stay out of jail

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:31.110
and they are going to try to drop it down

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:32.200
to a misdemeanor,

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:35.290
because I told the truth about everything,

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:37.580
and he was also

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:42.153
very,

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:45.683
he wasn't mad.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.880
- [Mark] The person you stabbed?

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:49.990
- Yes.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.840
So he was mad at the time,

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.390
but I don't think he's mad now.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:56.630
- [Mark] He was in court as well?

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:57.463
- No.

00:07:57.463 --> 00:07:58.296
- [Mark] Just you?

00:07:58.296 --> 00:07:59.470
- He's gonna be in court tomorrow, though.

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:00.830
- [Mark] So you have
another hearing tomorrow?

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:02.730
- Yes, but I know what's gonna happen.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:07.640
Is it okay if I say
something to him real quick?

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:08.473
- [Mark] Sure.

00:08:08.473 --> 00:08:09.486
- If he's watching, okay.

00:08:09.486 --> 00:08:10.319
I know we're not supposed
to talk or whatever,

00:08:10.319 --> 00:08:12.163
but if you're watching this, I am sorry.

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:14.603
It was wrong of me,

00:08:14.603 --> 00:08:17.980
and I wasn't in my right state of mind.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:18.840
- [Mark] Yes.

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:19.690
I think that's half your battle,

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:20.550
more than half your battle

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:22.650
is your mental state, right?

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:23.900
Whether it's drugs or alcohol,

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:25.848
or not taking your meds, or whatever.

00:08:25.848 --> 00:08:26.681
- Yeah.

00:08:26.681 --> 00:08:27.514
- [Mark] It seems like it's always

00:08:27.514 --> 00:08:29.298
some combination of those things.

00:08:29.298 --> 00:08:33.067
- Yeah.

00:08:33.067 --> 00:08:34.540
- [Mark] And so where does
your life go from here?

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:37.110
So you're not gonna be in jail or prison,

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:38.420
it looks like.

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:39.253
- No.

00:08:39.253 --> 00:08:40.330
- [Mark] So where do you go now?

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:43.920
- I go to,

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.230
I mean, I guess I just stay out

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:46.200
on the outs.

00:08:47.913 --> 00:08:48.860
- [Mark] On the street?

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:50.060
- Yeah.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:51.510
I'm gonna be staying at Ben's tonight,

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:54.010
and then tomorrow I'm
gonna go back to Hollywood

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:58.990
and try to get my IDs set
straight and everything.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:08:59.960
I think I'm gonna need a little help

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:00.910
getting my ID, but,

00:09:02.036 --> 00:09:03.910
and my social security income card,

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.212
and food stamps.

00:09:05.212 --> 00:09:08.680
- [Mark] And tell me about
the last couple weeks

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:13.664
of drug use, psych meds, and alcohol?

00:09:13.664 --> 00:09:16.020
- Oh, I haven't been on any alcohol.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:17.620
I haven't been drinking.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:18.783
Well, I drank one time.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:25.260
But I haven't been on drugs.

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:27.580
All I've been doing is
smoking weed and eating.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.100
Trying to figure out my ID.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:32.090
I had an appointment and
they didn't show up, so.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:32.923
- [Mark] That sounds like half

00:09:32.923 --> 00:09:33.987
of America right there.

00:09:33.987 --> 00:09:36.830
(laughing) That's what most
people your age are doing.

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:38.100
- It can't be that easy,

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:39.680
just to go to a library and have somebody

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:40.830
hook you up with an ID.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:44.340
- [Mark] Yeah, I'm not sure exactly

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:45.300
what your ID issues are,

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:46.846
but that sounds small compared to--

00:09:46.846 --> 00:09:47.709
- [Lin] Just to get a new one.

00:09:47.709 --> 00:09:48.542
- [Mark] Yeah, but.

00:09:48.542 --> 00:09:51.210
Yeah, nothing compared to
the court issues you were in.

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:52.043
- [Lin] No.

00:09:52.043 --> 00:09:54.665
- [Mark] So, and then
what do you think would be

00:09:54.665 --> 00:09:58.387
the most helpful step for you next?

00:09:58.387 --> 00:10:00.520
Get a job, go to rehab,

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:01.353
tell me what.

00:10:01.353 --> 00:10:02.380
Go see your mom in Florida?

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:04.950
- [Lin] I'd like to see my mom,

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.380
but it's not to that point yet.

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:09.000
I told her that I would be seeing her

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.350
after I get a place here.

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:12.710
That way she can come visit,

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:13.543
I can go there and visit,

00:10:13.543 --> 00:10:15.647
but I don't want to get
too comfortable there.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:22.700
Honestly, I mean I appreciate everybody

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:24.100
that's wanting to help, but I'm gonna try

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:25.150
to do this on my own.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:29.142
I think I can.

00:10:29.142 --> 00:10:29.975
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:10:29.975 --> 00:10:31.870
- [Lin] I might have a job.

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:32.703
- [Mark] Is that right?

00:10:32.703 --> 00:10:34.240
- [Lin] All I gotta do is apply at--

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:36.080
- [Mark] Because you mentioned that, the--

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:36.913
- [Lin] Huh?

00:10:36.913 --> 00:10:37.746
- [Mark] You mentioned
that in the last talk,

00:10:37.746 --> 00:10:40.080
that you might have a job opportunity.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:40.913
- [Lin] For which one?

00:10:40.913 --> 00:10:41.910
- [Mark] I forget which one.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.690
It was a restaurant,
or something like that?

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:44.630
- [Lin] Uh, Porta Potty?

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:46.553
- [Mark] (laughing) no, it wasn't that.

00:10:46.553 --> 00:10:47.386
(Lin laughing)

00:10:47.386 --> 00:10:48.219
